  "worked_solution": "To express the equation of the parabola in vertex form, we need to complete the square. \n\nFirst, we take out a factor of $7$ from the entire expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{x}^{2}-28x+18 & =7({x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{18}{7})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2}-{2}^{2}+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot x+{2}^{2})-{2}^{2}+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-4+\\frac{18}{7} & = \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-\\frac{10}{7} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute this result back into our original expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7({x}^{2}-4x+\\frac{18}{7}) & = \\\\ 7((x-2)^{2}-\\frac{10}{7}) & = \\\\ 7(x-2)^{2}-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, expressed in vertex form, the equation of the parabola is $y=7(x-2)^{2}-10.$",
